# Undisclosed label system

Use `data/UD_Peptide_Label_Catalog.xlsx` as the editable source of truth and run `npm run sync` after workbook edits.

## Locked brand assets

- Latest UD brand mark: `assets/brand/UD_Brand_Mark_Latest_Original.png`
- Mascot: `assets/brand/UD_Sentinel_Mascot_Original.png`
- Keep both originals unchanged. Use the included transparent production derivatives; do not redraw, substitute, distort, or add a background box.
- Both assets are already embedded in the SVG masters for portable printing.
- Default `BRAND_GAP_CHARS` is 1 and may be changed from 0 through 4.

## Locked label design

- White stock, black-only ink.
- No outside printed border.
- Full-bleed black rail on the left physical edge.
- Vertical company name and brand mark centered in the rail.
- Centered `— UNDISCLOSED —` header.
- Product name and amount bar centered in the middle panel.
- Mascot behind and above the QR box; larger proportionally on 50×30.
- Same QR/legal panel on every template.
- Replace values only inside elements marked by `data-field` or `{{FIELD}}`.
- Never move the rail, center panel, amount bar, dividers, QR panel, mascot anchor, or safety margins.

## Sizes and printer

- 3 mL vial: 40×20 mm, 472×236 px at 300 DPI.
- 10 mL vial: 50×30 mm, 591×354 px at 300 DPI.
- Export monochrome one-bit PNG. Do not scale, crop, fit-to-page, enhance, or add an outline.

## Fields

All fields in `config/label-system.json` are editable. This includes company/header text, peptide name, amount, unit, storage, form, calculator headers and values, legal lines, QR value/toggle, mascot toggle, and brand spacing.

Use `IU` for HGH, HCG, HMG, EPO, and other IU products. Do not force every product to MG.

## QR targets

- If a peptide/strength has a COA URL, its label QR must open that COA.
- QR priority is: COA URL, explicit QR URL override, then `https://www.wellpept.com`.
- Keep `COA URL` in the workbook when available; vendor COAs imported by the catalog sync follow the same priority.

## Vial placement

- Use only the stock black-cap vial images in `assets/vials/`.
- Labels sit below the neck and cover 60% of the straight body.
- Leave 20% exposed glass above and 20% below.
- Derive label placement from each vial profile's straight `bodyBoundsPx`: top = body top + 20%, height = 60% of body height, bottom clearance = 20%. Never add or use a separate hard-coded `labelBoundsPx`; this rule applies to 3 mL, 10 mL, and every future size.
- Preserve the round black flip top, brushed-silver crimp, vial geometry, powder amount, powder texture, and pure black background.
- KLOW, GLOW, GHK-Cu, and AHK-Cu use the cobalt-blue cake unless the workbook overrides the visual.
- Both 3 mL stock images must remain identical except for peptide cake color.
- Trim all paper edges evenly. Never leave a white perimeter, tab, nub, torn corner, or bottom-right sliver.

## Required verification

Run `npm run build`. Do not treat the update as finished unless `validation-report.json` says `PASS`.
